{
  "version": 1,
  "about": "The drawn jog display's messages (#455): each state and the exact bytes on the WD port. The Swift encoder (Kit tests) and the C decoder (firmware tests) both walk this file. Host to unit: F0 00 02 0B 7F 10 <cmd> <len hi> <len lo> <op> <args> F7, len counting op and args (14 bits). Unit to host: the reply header F0 00 02 0B 01 10 instead. cmd 0x20 is a placeholder until #466 finds a number the stock dispatcher leaves free. Ops: 00 capability, 01 begin, 02 end, 03 deck; 04-0B are reserved for text, tempo, time, state, beat, needle, meter, phase. Colors go as two 7-bit bytes per channel, high then low. Player: 0 empty, 1 track, 2 OSC clip, 3 MIDI clip, 4 sequencer, 5 other. Each op has one exact length (capability 2, begin 2, end 2, deck 9, counting the op); any other is ignored, as is version 0. Entries with \"direction\": \"unit\" go from the unit to the host; the rest from the host.",
